#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:52
msgid "LET'S GET STARTED!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:54
msgid "In this tour, you practice adding a new tile source with one-way platforms to your tileset."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:57
msgid "You'll build upon what you learned in Tour 103 to add mushroom platforms that the character can jump through and stand on."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:74
msgid "Adding more tile sources"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:77
msgid "In the previous tours, you learned how to add a tile source and set up a physics layer with collision shapes on your tiles. You added collision shapes to every tile."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:78
msgid "You can add multiple tile sources to a tileset and add collision shapes and change their properties more selectively."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:79
msgid "Let's build upon what you learned and go one step further."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:86
msgid "Challenge: add a mushroom tile source"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:89
msgid "Your mission, if you accept it, is to add and configure a new tile source to your tile set: mushroom platforms with a cap that the player can jump through."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:90
msgid "This time, I will not guide you every step of the way. Instead, you will have to use what you learned in the previous tours to achieve this goal."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:91
msgid "To begin the challenge, let's make sure you have the [b]Ground[/b] node selected in the scene tree and open the [b]TileSet editor[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:99
msgid "Open the TileSet editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:108
msgid "Adding the mushroom tile source"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:111
msgid "Your first task is to add the mushroom tile source to your tileset resource and create tiles for every part of the mushrooms."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:112
msgid "The editor can create tiles for you automatically by selecting [b]Yes[/b] in the dialog that appears when you add a tile source."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:118
msgid "Add the [b]mushroom.png[/b] tile source to the tileset"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:134
msgid "Create tiles for every part of the mushroom"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:158
msgid "Adding a collision shape to the mushroom cap tiles"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:161
msgid "Great job! Now that you have added the mushroom tile source, it's time to add a collision shape to the mushroom cap tiles. The cap tiles are the top row of the mushroom tile source."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:162
msgid "Be sure to [b]only add the collision shape to the mushroom cap tiles[/b], not the stem!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:167
msgid "Turn on the Select tool in the Tileset editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:174
msgid "Add collision shapes to the mushroom cap tiles"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:202
msgid "Setting up one-way collisions"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:205
msgid "You now have a collision shape on the mushroom cap tiles, but by default it's solid and the player cannot jump through it from below."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:206
msgid "To set up one-way collisions, expand the [b]Polygon 0[/b] and turn on the one-way collision property. This will turn selected tiles into one-way platforms."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:211
msgid "Set up one-way collisions on the mushroom cap tiles"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:235
msgid "Try it out!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:238
msgid "Try painting a mushroom cap tile above a platform in the viewport! Open the [b]TileMap editor[/b] and select the mushroom cap tile."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:239
msgid "In the TileMap editor, select the [b]Paint tool[/b] and click and drag over the mushroom tiles to select them all."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:240
msgid "Then, [b]Left-Click[/b] in the viewport to stamp the entire mushroom at once."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:241
msgid "Right-click in the viewport to erase tiles if you make a mistake."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:247
msgid "Open the TileMap editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:254
msgid "Paint a mushroom in the level"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:270
msgid "Run the scene"
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:273
msgid "Give the scene a try! Press the [b]Play Current Scene[/b] button in the top right corner of the editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/104_one_way_collisions/104_one_way_collisions.gd:274
msgid "You should be able to jump through the mushroom cap tiles from below and stand on them. If you misplaced the mushroom cap tiles and platforms, go back to the previous step and try again."
